/* Learning Data: Governance principles, in English: the words of the series' labs (training) and scenarios (evaluation), for the
   prologue (film 0) and its ten films. Keep the keys in step with learn.es.js. assets/data-governance/learn.js draws them; "vis"
   names a picture in its PIX, which takes its words from the lab (w) or the scenario (st).
   site-tools/build_series.py reads this file as text (series_learn): "labs:[" and "qs:[" each start a line; each lab's first keys
   are id, kind, film, chapter (a chapter id of its film), c and name, in that order, its id made of letters, digits and _ only; each
   scenario's are type, n (its film's number times ten, plus its place: the prologue's are 1 to 9), lab and film. No other object
   here starts with an id, and no other key is called kind or starts an object with type (they're counted).
   The series' first part: papers and people, never code, file paths or tool screens; words such as change request, check and table.
   Names, numbers and dates follow each film's narration: check a film's labs and scenarios against it when it changes.
   close: the series' last words, under the scenarios' results for all films and for the last film: that film's closing chapter
   (chapter), in its own words, and in learn.es.js in its Spanish captions. */
